Add a public custom-attribute API

LittleFS user attributes are the idiomatic place for POSIX-style metadata --
SPEC.md describes them as intended for "timestamps, hashes", they ride the
entry's metadata so rename moves them and delete drops them, and this port
already uses one ('t') for mtime.

But nothing outside the port can reach them. `_efs[]` is file-scope static,
esp_littlefs_by_label() is static, and littlefs_api.h -- where esp_littlefs_t.fs
lives -- is under PRIV_INCLUDE_DIRS. ESP-IDF's VFS cannot route around it
either, having no chmod or attribute member in esp_vfs_fs_ops_t (IDF's own
vfs/test_apps/main/test_vfs_access.c carries a TODO saying as much).

So a project wanting to store, say, a file mode has no way to put it on the
file. These three functions are modelled directly on the port's existing
esp_littlefs_update_mtime_attr()/esp_littlefs_get_mtime_attr(), taking the same
sem_take(efs) lock and the same label lookup.

Paths are mount-relative, matching the rest of the internal API.

